# XSH isprint() and isprint_l()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The tests run in the POSIX locale (setlocale(LC_ALL, "C")); only the
# portable character set is examined. The _l forms are tested with a locale
# object from newlocale() for "C"; a failure to make one is UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XSH.isprint.001
anchor     functions/isprint.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isprint.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
since      1988
says       In the POSIX locale isprint() returns non-zero for each portable
           character of the class as the locale definition lists it: the
           letters, the ten digits, the 32 punctuation characters and the
           space. Checked through the function and through the header form.
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.isprint.002
anchor     functions/isprint.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isprint.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
since      1988
says       In the POSIX locale isprint() returns 0 for each portable character
           the locale definition does not place in the class: the portable
           control characters (the null character, alert, backspace, tab,
           newline, vertical-tab, form-feed, carriage-return).
note       Only the portable characters are examined; other control codes,
           bytes above 127 and values outside the domain are unspecified or
           undefined.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.isprint.003
anchor     functions/isprint.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isprint.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       isprint(EOF) is inside the domain and returns 0, since EOF is not a
           character of the class.
test       t/003-eof.c

assertion  XSH.isprint.004
anchor     functions/isprint.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isprint.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
since      2008
says       isprint_l() with a locale object for the POSIX locale gives the same
           answers as isprint() for the portable characters: non-zero for the
           members, 0 for the others.
note       The locale object comes from newlocale(); UNRESOLVED if it cannot be
           made.
test       t/004-locale-object.c

assertion  XSH.isprint.005
anchor     functions/isprint.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isprint.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2008
says       isprint_l(EOF, locale) with a locale object for the POSIX locale
           returns 0.
test       t/005-locale-eof.c
